\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Ringgit outperforms; peso, baht checked by c.banks\b0\par\par\uc2 697 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2009\par 07:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Ringgit outperforms in Asia as dollar loses ground\par \par \uc2 * Investors dump U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Australian jobs data\par \par \uc2 * Thai c.bank confirms \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rising too fast\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  suspected to curb gains in peso, won\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Oct 8 (Reuters) - The Malaysian ringgit led Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher as the dollar faltered after Australian jobs data boosted investor optimism about the world economy, but gains in the peso and baht were curbed by central banks.\par \par \uc2 South Korea's authority was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the won's rally after Australia's stronger-than-expected employment data supported optimism and led investors to dump the U.S. dollar. [ID:nT358966] [IDnSEO369844]\par \par \uc2 China's markets remained shut for a week-long holiday\par \par \uc2 RINGGIT, SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The ringgit <MYR=> jumped 0.8 percent to 3.388 per dollar, its highest since August 2008, while the Singapore dollar <SGD=> followed the firmer tone.\par \par \uc2 "U.S. dollar/Singapore dollar broke lower after the shocking Australian jobs data. It was the same story for U.S. dollar/ringgit," said a Kuala Lumpur-based trader.\par \par \uc2 Singapore dollar gains 0.4 percent to 1.3935 to the U.S. dollar, highest since early 2008, but traders saw no sign of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday to defend the key 1.4 level.\par \par \uc2 PESO\par \par \uc2 The <PHP=> gained a third of a percent to 46.45 per dollar, highest so far this year, but it faced strong resistance at the level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen defending.\par \par \uc2 "BSP (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is soaking up all the dollar selling at the year-low level," said a Manila-based dealer, who estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $350-400 million.\par \par \uc2 One-month offshore dollar/peso non-deliverable forwards <PHPNDFOR=> briefly eased to 46.45, implying no change from the spot.\par \par \uc2 "The one-month NDFs have traded as low as par on the offshore market and players are fully convinced that 46.45 will break and a new year low will be established soon," added the dealer.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 The baht <THB=> rose a fifth of a percent to a new 14-month high at 33.28 per dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars.\par \par \uc2 The bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rising too fast and that it would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , prompting the baht to steady near 32.29. [ID:nBKT001108]\par \par \uc2 "We believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has entered the market slowly this morning but it was not that active," said a dealer at a Thai bank.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently in recent weeks to curb the baht's strength amid concerns about exports, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Still, the baht has gained 2 percent against dollar since early September as foreign money flows into the stock market. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at