\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 573 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2009\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ASIA CENTRAL BANKS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AGAIN AS DOLLAR TUMBLES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar continued to tumble against most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday, prompting another wave of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by central banks in South Korea, Taiwan, and the Philippines seeking to limit damage to their export industries. (published 0343 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIA JOBS SURGE BOOSTS RBA HIKE EXPECTATIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The number of employed Australians surged in September, defying economists' expectations of a fall and firming up expectations of more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  interest rate increases this year. (published 0237 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN AUG CURR ACCT SURPLUS UP, BUT LOW RATES DRAG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's current account surplus rose slightly less than expected in August, as low interest rates overseas and the strong yen ate into Japanese firms' investment earnings, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0213 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN SEP CORP BANKRUPTCY CASES DOWN 15.7% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following data on Japanese corporate bankruptcies in September are from private credit research agency Teikoku Databank Ltd. (published 0430 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA GOVT: WILL STICK TO EXPANSIONARY FISCAL POLICY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government will stick to its expansionary fiscal policy for the time being as private sector activity continues to be tepid and the strength of the global economy's recovery remains uncertain, the Ministry of Strategy and Finance said Thursday. (published 0115 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA GOVT:TO LIMIT STATE-RUN COS FROM SEEKING FUNDS OVERSEAS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government will limit state-run firms from seeking dollar-funding overseas in a bid to slow the won's rise against the greenback, a senior official at the Ministry of Strategy and Finance said Thursday. (published 0540 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 THAILAND CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : HAVE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENED\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET RECENTLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday that it has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market recently because the baht has been too strong against its fundamentals since early this month. (published 0557 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SINGTEL OPTUS LOOKING TO SELL 10-YR BENCHMARK USD BOND-SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singtel Optus Pty Ltd. is looking to sell a 10-year benchmark U.S. dollar bond and aims to price the debt this week, a person familiar with the deal said Thursday. (published 0148 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: LUMENA RESOURCES TO SELL MAIDEN GLOBAL US DOLLAR BOND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese minerals company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lumena Resources Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it is looking to sell its first-ever global U.S. dollar bond to repay debt and finance its expansion. (published 0304 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI SEPTEMBER CONSUMER CONFIDENCE INDEX 75.6 VS 74.5 AUGUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Consumer confidence in Thailand improved in September for a fourth straight month, due mainly to lower oil prices and the government's economic stimulus package. (published 0358 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS: OPTIONS UP AS MKT BRACES FOR DLR BELOW Y88 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen options rose in Asia Thursday as growing speculation that the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would soon fall below Y88.00 increased demand for hedges against further dollar weakness. (published 0341 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =OFF THE RUN: REPO MARKET ACTIVITY WON'T COME SURGING BACK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The crucial fixed-income securities lending market is recovering from the woes of the financial crisis, but it may never return to its former self. (published 1925 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =IN THE MONEY: MORE EVIDENCE OF SOME BAD TARP DECISIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Here's more evidence the Treasury Department wasn't always smart about deciding which banks got bailout funds. (published 2012 GMT) [ 08-10-09 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091008e5a80006z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
