\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Thai competitiveness not hurt by firm baht-Fin Min\b0\par\par\uc2 251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2009\par 08:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, detail)\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Oct 5 (Reuters) - Gains in Thailand's baht, the third-strongest performer among Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, have not eroded Thai trade competitiveness, Finance Minister Korn Chatikavanij told reporters on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The baht, tracking bullish Asian peers in appreciating against a weakening dollar in recent weeks, rose about another 0.27 percent on Monday. It has gained 4.13 percent against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year.\par \par \uc2 "Baht has appreciated in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and our trade competitors have not gained any advantage over us. Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are all now on a sustained bullish trend," Korn told reporters in a telephone briefing.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOT) has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly through offshore bank agents to curb baht gains this year, helping to push Thai foreign reserves to $132.3 billion on Sept. 25 from $111 billion at the end of 2008.\par \par \uc2 The baht has appreciated about 1.74 percent against the dollar since Sept. 10 to trade at around 33.42 on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tried to hold the baht back largely by committing to buy dollars through forward \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps. Latest weekly data showed outstanding dollar/baht swap contracts rose to $14.2 billion on Sept. 25 from $7.2 billion on June 5. [ID:nBKT001103]\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kitiphong Thaichareon; Writing by Vithoon Amorn; Editing by Jason Szep)\par \par \uc2 THAILAND-ECONOMY/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091005e5a5000cg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
