\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah up on \uc2 Moody's\uc2 ; won, baht at 1-year highs\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lee Chyen Yee   \par \uc2 618 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2009\par 04:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TAIPEI, Sept 16 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened on Wednesday, with the rupiah <IDR=>, won <KRW=> and baht <THB=> near one-year highs as better than expected U.S. retail sales and manufacturing data spurred investors into riskier assets.\par \par \uc2 However, traders said the central banks of South Korea and \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying U.S. dollars to keep gains in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in check.\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah rose to 9,765 to the U.S. dollar, the highest level since October last year, helped by \uc2 Moody's\uc2  raising the country's sovereign rating to Ba2 from Ba3 due to its economic resilience and upbeat growth prospects. [ID:nWNA3503]\par \par \uc2 The rupiah, which is Asia's best performer this year with a near 13 percent gain against the dollar, was capped by dollar demand from importers ahead of a long holiday weekend that stretches from Friday to next Wednesday. Traders said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far. [ID:nSP535844]\par \par \uc2 "The major theme today is a weakening global U.S. dollar," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actions vary from country to country. In certain countries, they are supporting the U.S. dollar to help their exports, but for others like Indonesia, they are trying seek a stronger local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to go against inflation stress."\par \par \uc2 Implied volatility on the rupiah <IDRVOL> remained low, with the one-month volatility quoted at just 9 percent, compared with more than 20 percent earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 WON, BAHT\par \par \uc2 The South Korean won rose to around 1,207 to the dollar, the strongest since October last year.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was buying U.S. dollars to limit the rise in an effort to ensure exports of technology gadgets, autos and steel remain competitive.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the Bank of Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth rather than to reverse the USD/KRW decline," \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  said in a report.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the won's short-term risk reversals were close to favouring won call options despite the Bank of Korea's suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nSP530905]\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the baht rose to 33.70 per dollar, a one-year high, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suspected of having \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb its strength. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at   0712 GMT\par  Change on the day at   0712 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        90.59          91.03       +0.49\par  Sing dlr        1.4146         1.4187       +0.29\par  Taiwan dlr      32.510         32.637       +0.39\par  Korean won     1210.15        1218.50       +0.69\par  Baht             33.75          33.88       +0.39\par  Peso             48.34          48.34       +0.00\par  Rupiah         9765.00        9885.00       +1.23\par  Rupee            48.33          48.64       +0.63\par  Ringgit         3.4800         3.5000       +0.57\par  Yuan            6.8269         6.8289  