\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won rises with stocks, baht weighed down by c.bank\b0\par\par\uc2 643 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2009\par 09:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Won rises on inflows, charts point to further gains\par \par \uc2 * Baht falls as traders suspect dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * China stocks sold off amid jitters about liquidity steps\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Aug 6 (Reuters) - The South Korean won rose on Thursday as foreign investors bought into a local stock rally, while the Thai baht fell on suspected dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at containing the unit's strength.\par \par \uc2 Asian stocks inched up but shares in Shanghai fell as much as 3 percent, weighed by speculation Chinese authorities may take more steps to rein in liquidity amid concerns about asset bubbles. [ID:nL6709717]\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> gained 0.4 percent to 1,218.9 per dollar in step with local stocks, and charts pointed to further gains despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the won broke key resistance around 1,220 -- a 61.8% Fibonacci retracement of its fall between July 2008 and its decade-low hit in Marchn -- suggesting further gains in the Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Technically, dollar/won is down unless it reclaims 1,240," said a Singapore-based dealer. "We don't see much technical support for dollar until 1,170."\par \par \uc2 The won has gained a torrid 28 percent since March.\par \par \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  said in a note earlier this week that the won may ease to 1,250 in 3 months, but it could regain steam to 1,200 and 1,150 in 6 to 12-months due to the spill-over from China's economic stimulus and fund inflows into Korea's markets.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=TH> lost a quarter of a percent to 33.99 per dollar as traders suspected mild dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the local unit's strength.\par \par \uc2 "BOT was buying the dollar to slow the baht's appreciation," said a trader in Bangkok. Traders spotted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar bids from 33.97-33.98.\par \par \uc2 The baht has been confined in a tight range since early June due to official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but is still up almost 7 percent from early March.\par \par \uc2 Three-month implied volatilities in the baht <THBVOL> edged up to 5.3 percent from 4 percent, but they were still down from as high as 8 percent in March.\par \par \uc2 The suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to aid the country's struggling exporters came as Primer Minister Abhisit Vejjajiva said that the worst is over for Thailand's economy. [ID:nBKK74521] \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at   0639 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        95.11          94.91       -0.21\par  Sing dlr        1.4326         1.4340       +0.10\par  Taiwan dlr      32.715         32.720       +0.02\par  Korean won     1223.00        1224.30       +0.11\par  Baht             33.98          33.90       -0.22\par  Peso             47.77          47.84       +0.16\par  Rupiah         9895.00        9870.00       -0.25\par  Rupee            47.59          47.52       -0.15\par  Ringgit         3.4900         3.4950       +0.14\par  Yuan            6.8307         6.8309       +0.00\par  Change so far in 2009\pa