\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  fears hurt Thai baht, Singapore dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 580 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 2009\par 07:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Thai baht falls on fears of possible c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Singapore dollar eases, further weakness expected\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, June 29 (Reuters) - The Thai baht fell on Monday on caution over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the unit to help exporters, while most of its regional peers also eased slightly in tandem with Asian stocks.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar regained some ground against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  <.DXY> after falling broadly late last week on a renewed call by China for a super-sovereign reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nT358330]\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=TH> fell about 0.4 percent to 34.13 per dollar as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained broadly and market participants fretted about possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the local unit.\par \par \uc2 "I haven't seen BOT in the market today but think they will buy dollars at 34," said a trader in Bangkok.\par \par \uc2 Traders have suspected sporadic dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent sessions to prevent the unit, which has gained 6 percent since early March, from strengthening beyond 34 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Thailand's Finance Ministry forecast that the economy would shrink 2.5-3.5 percent this year, and Ekniti Nitithanprapas, a spokesman for the ministry's fiscal policy office, said a weaker baht will help the economy more than lower interest rates. [ID:nBKK508486]\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> eased a tad to 1.4558 per U.S. dollar as investors treaded cautiously amid persistent fears of possible official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some traders reckon the Singapore dollar is close to the upper end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's undisclosed trade-weighted band.\par \par \uc2 "We see higher U.S. dollar/Singapore dollar and are also biased to sell Singapore dollar/Malaysian ringgit," said a trader in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 Malaysian ringgit eased to 2.4298 per Singapore dollar <SGDMYR=R> from Friday's close at 2.4263.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at OCBC Bank say they expect Singapore dollar to fall to 1.4720 against the U.S. dollar by the end of September, before rebounding to 1.4480 by the end of 2009. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0522 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        95.38          95.22       -0.17\par  Sing dlr        1.4539         1.4545       +0.04\par  Taiwan dlr      32.919         32.925       +0.02\par  Korean won     1288.30        1284.30       -0.31\par  Baht             34.04          33.98       -0.18\par  Peso             48.30          48.31       +0.02\par  Rupiah        10240.00       10220.00       -0.20\par  Rupee            48.14          48.09       -0.09\par  Ringgit         3.5330         3.5300       -0.08\par  Yuan            6.8340         6.8338       -0.00\par  Change so far in 2009\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        95.38      