\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Thai c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  on baht, may act again\b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 2009\par 08:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Will act on baht volatility\par \par \uc2 * Baht still competitive for trade\par \par \uc2 * Baht could weaken after economy recovers, imports rise (Adds more details from press conference)\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, June 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the baht's rise on Wednesday, and said it would act again to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's volatility.\par \par \uc2 "We have done something on the baht which has gained in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Bank of Thailand Assistant Governor Suchada Kirakul told reporters as the baht <THB=> traded at an eight-month high.\par \par \uc2 Suchada did not give more details, but a dealer in Singapore said the BoT bought dollars on Wednesday to defend the 34 baht-per-dollar level.\par \par \uc2 Suchada said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would act again if necessary.\par \par \uc2 "We will act on baht volatility, but we also need to take care of several sectors such as exporters, importers and the people. We have to maintain a balance," she said.\par \par \uc2 Thailand's foreign resevers rose to $120.5 billion as of May 22, from $118.5 billion on May 15.\par \par \uc2 The government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have come under pressure from Thai businesses in the past two weeks to take action on the baht.\par \par \uc2 Suchada said exporters and importers had to adjust and should not always bet on a one-way movement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The baht traded at around 34.03 per dollar on Wednesday, after hitting 33.92 in early trade. It has risen about 3 percent since April.\par \par \uc2 Thai exports -- equivalent to 60 percent of gross domestic product each year -- fell 25.2 percent in April on the year, but industrial production showed signs that the worst was over for the economy, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed. [ID:nBKK400845]. However, Suchada said the baht was likely to weaken in the future when the economy started to recover and imports increased. ($1=34.03 Baht)\par \par \uc2 THAILAND-ECONOMY/BAHT (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090603e5630009o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
