\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won at 6-month high; Thai c.bank seen capping baht\b0\par\par\uc2 721 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2009\par 05:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Won at 6-month peak, leads Asian rally vs weaker dollar\par \par \uc2  * Thai baht jumps, prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  * Singapore dollar rises but trails regional peers\par \par \uc2  By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 11 (Reuters) - The South Korean won led most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to multi-month highs versus the dollar on Monday on signs of a global economic recovery, triggering the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the local unit's strength.\par \par \uc2  Signs of improvements in the global economy, reinforced by data showing smaller-than-expected U.S. job losses in April, boosted Asian stocks while the dollar hit a four-month low against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nSP21723] [ID:nT43914]\par \par \uc2  WON\par \par \uc2  The South Korean won jumped 1.3 percent to 1,230.8 per dollar, its highest since October 31. It later pulled back to 1,235 amid fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  On Friday, traders suspected the authorities were buying dollars in the market to curb further rise in the won, which has rebounded 20 percent since hitting a 11-year low on March 6.\par \par \uc2  Some traders expected the won to test the key 1,200 level in the near term, but they also cautioned about further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the country's struggling exporters.\par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar/won non-deliverable forwards curved shifted lower but failed to match the spot's sharp move.\par \par \uc2  One-year dollar/won NDFs <KRWNDFOR=> fell to 1,217.9, implying a 1.2 percent won appreciation from the spot compared to 2.4 percent on Friday.\par \par \uc2  BAHT\par \par \uc2  The Thai baht <THB=TH> gained 0.8 percent to 34.58 per  dollar -- its highest since late December, even as traders cited modest \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise.\par \par \uc2   "The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been capping the baht's gains, but is not aggressive," said a trader in Singapore.\par \par \uc2   A Bangkok-based trader also suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was buying dollars near 34.80 to limit the baht's strength.\par \par \uc2  The baht has gained 4 percent since early March, part of an Asia-wide \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rally fuelled by tentative signs of global economic recovery.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar <SGD=> gained 0.2 percent to 1.4562 per U.S. dollar, its highest since January 5, as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened broadly.\par \par \uc2  But the Singapore dollar's gains still trailed those in most regional peers as investors feared its recent strength may trigger official dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  "U.S. houses and funds are still selling U.S. dollars non stop despite on-and-off rumours the authority will buy USD," said a Singapore-based trader.\par \par \uc2  Singapore dollar has gained 6 percent since early March.\par \par \uc2  Investors fear that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which lowered the centre of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trade-weighted band in April to help spur the recession-hit economy, might move to tame the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0525 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        98.43          98.55       +0.12\par  Sing dlr        1.4580         1.4590       +0.07\par  Taiwan dlr      32.842         33.040       +0.60\par  Korean won     1235.40        1247.00       +0.94\par  Baht             34.65          34.86       +0.61\par  Peso             47.05          47.25       +0.43\par  Rupiah        10270.00       10370.00       +0.97\par  Rupee            49.18          49.27       +0.18\par  Ringgit         3.5000         3.5150       +0.43\par  Yuan            6.8217         6.8218       +0.00\par  Change so far in 2009\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        98.43          90.60       -7.95\par  Sing dlr        1.4580         1.4340       -1.65\par  Taiwan dlr      32.842         32.860       +0.05\par  Korean won     1235.40        1259.50       +1.95\par  Baht             34.65          34.80       +0.43\par  Peso             47.05          47.52       +1.00\par  Rupiah        10270.00       11000.00       +7.11\par  Rupee            49.18          48.71       -0.96\par  Ringgit         3.5000         3.4500       -1.43\par  Yuan            6.8217         6.8230       +0.02\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  (Reporting by Kevin Yao; Editing by Kazunori Takada)\par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090514e55b0006l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
