\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Thai baht in line, govt borrowing manageable-c.bank\b0\par\par\uc2 397 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2009\par 10:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, May 7 (Reuters) - Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Thursday the Thai baht remained competitive, noting it moved in line with other strengthening Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The baht rose about 0.40 percent against the dollar on Thursday. It has lost about 0.54 percent against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year.\par \par \uc2 The head of the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2 , Tarisa Watanagase, added at a stock exchange seminar that the Thai market could easily accommodate further government borrowing without crowding out private borrowers.\par \par \uc2 The governor estimated that the Thai banking sector had over 1 trillion baht ($28.6 billion) of surplus liquidity.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Korn Chatikavanij said in Singapore on Thursday the domestic market could absorb government plans to borrow up to 800 billion baht between now and 2011.\par \par \uc2 He said the local funds being raised by the authorities would go toward financing fiscal deficits and government stimulus spendings planned for the next three years.\par \par \uc2 The Thai cabinet approved plans on Wednesday to borrow the amount as part of a government policy to bolster the economy hit by the global downturn.\par \par \uc2 "There's not much concern we can raise the money domestically without impacting significantly on the yield curve," Korn said at an investment seminar in Singapore organised by \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Thai bond yields rose by 5 to 10 basis points across the board early on Thursday on the government's borrowing plans, traders said. [ID:nBKK416014]\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by buying about 9 billion baht worth of 5-year and 10-year bonds that helped ease the bond yields in late afternoon trading, they said.\par \par \uc2 Investors largely ignored Korn's comments that the market can absorb the additional borrowings, they said. [ID:nSIN402736]\par \par \uc2 "The yields stabilised on the back of the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not because of the finance minister's statements. What the market needs is clarity and details of their borrowing plans," a trader said.\par \par \uc2 The yield on the five-year bond <TH5YT=RR> eased to 2.48/2.52 percent by late afternoon from 2.50/2.55 percent before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kitiphong Thaichareon; Writing by Vithoon Amorn;\par \par \uc2 THAILAND-ECONOMY/TARISA (UPDATE 1)(attn neil)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090507e557000xx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
