\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia mostly firmer but capped by Mumbai attacks\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kevin Yao   \par \uc2 735 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2008\par 06:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Nov 27 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose on Thursday in tandem with firmer stocks, but the positive sentiment was contained by the deadly attacks in India's financial hub Mumbai and Thailand's political strife.\par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> gained 1 percent to 12,150 per dollar, helped by suspected dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The rupiah open at 12,150, Bank Indonesia was briefly in the market," said a trader in Jakarta.\par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso <PHP=> rose as far as 48.82 per dollar, up 0.6 percent from Wednesday's close.\par \par \uc2 It later pulled back to 48.93 as Indian commandos and armed police laid siege to gunmen holding foreigners hostage after attacks that killed at least 101 people. [ID:nSP355003]\par \par \uc2 "The unrest in India and Thailand tends to support risk aversion," said a trader in Manila.\par \par \uc2 Stocks in the Asia-Pacific region outside of Japan <.MIAPJ0000PUS> rose 2.8 percent, set for a fifth straight day of gains, helped by China's hefty interest rate cut.\par \par \uc2 India's financial markets are shut on Thursday, but analysts expect the Indian rupee <INR=IN> to come under selling pressures in the near term due to the Mumbai attacks.\par \par \uc2 "This will be negative for the rupee/dollar, but again I want to stress that the impact will be short-lived," said Joseph Tan, Asia chief economist at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 OCBC \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Enrico Tanuwidjaja said he believed foreign funds may hold inflows to India for the time being.\par \par \uc2 "The Reserve Bank of India is likely to guard the dollar/rupee on possible spikes," he added.\par \par \uc2 The rupee, one of the worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia with a year-to-day loss of 20 percent against the dollar, closed at 49.48 on Wednesday after hitting a 10-day high at 49.25.\par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=TH> fell as low as 35.38 per dollar, its weakest level since February 2007 as pressures built on \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's military to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help contain widespread civil unrest. [ID:nBKK345814].\par \par \uc2 The Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS> inched down to 6.83 per dollar amid concerns about a sharp slowdown in the economy despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sharpest interest rate cut in a decade.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  late on Wednesday slashed benchmark one-year lending and deposit rates by 1.08 percentage point, bringing the cost of one-year borrowing to 5.58 percent. It also said it would cut banks' reserve ratios by between 1 and 2 percentage points on Dec. 5. [ID:nPEK95037]\par \par \uc2 "The authorities cannot do much about export demand, though we continue to expect them to allow the renminbi to depreciate a bit against the U.S. dollar," said analysts at ING in a note.\par \par \uc2 The yuan has been kept steady since July and most analysts expect it to be kept on such tight leash in the near term.\par \par \uc2 Zhang Ping, chairman of the National Development and Reform Commission, who told a news conference on Thursday that China would stick to its present \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. [ID:nBJC000230] \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0524 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 