\par\par \b \uc2 BIS-UPDATE 1-Thai c.bank to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  if baht becomes volatile\b0\par\par\uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2008\par 17:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, background)\par \par \uc2 BASEL, Sept 7 (Reuters) - Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no exchange-rate target but would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the baht became very volatile, its deputy governor Atchana Waiquamdee said on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in the Swiss city of Basel, she also said Thailand's political crisis, coupled with slowing major developed economies, would weigh on the country's growth in the second half of this year.\par \par \uc2 Investor sentiment on Thailand has been deteriorating after Prime Minister Samak Sundaravej imposed emergency rule last week which failed to lead to the eviction of thousands of protesters occupying his official compound.\par \par \uc2 The main stock index <.SETI> hit a 19-month low last week while the baht <THB=TH> hit a one-year low of 34.6 to the dollar on Friday, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Losses were aggravated by the general investor aversion to risky emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped further, Atchana told reporters: "Our exchange rate hasn't been changed. We don't have any target, for the exchange rate level, but when it's very volatile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may step in."\par \par \uc2 The political turmoil in Thailand was a risk factor but had not yet deteriorated to the point that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed to cut its growth forecast of between 4.8 and 5.8 percent for this year, she said.\par \par \uc2 "Up until now, we don't think it (political instability) is going to have an impact on our growth forecast," Atchana said.\par \par \uc2 "If it is prolonged for the next month or two, especially in the high season of tourism, it will have some impact."\par \par \uc2 The economic slowdown in G3 countries and Thai political instability would also put the brake on growth for the remainder of the year.\par \par \uc2 "Unfortunately the internal factor will become one of the negative factors that will drag on growth in the second half," she said.\par \par \uc2 Atchana said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials attending the two-day meeting at the Bank for International Settlements are focused on the rising dollar at a time when data showed the U.S. economy was slowing, and Monday's gathering will discuss this issue.\par \par \uc2 "What we are talking about is the dollar gaining some strength even though the U.S. economy's statistics that (have) come out lately showed we couldn't avoid an economic slowdown in the U.S.," she said.\par \par \uc2 "However, exports in Asia (are) holding up quite well." (Reporting by Tamora Vidaillet; Writing by Natsuko Waki; Editing by Quentin Bryar)\par \par \uc2 BIS-THAILAND/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ABX|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080907e497000du\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
