\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia dips further on credit worries, strong dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 By Melissa Chia   \par \uc2 737 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2008\par 10:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Aug 26 (Reuters) - The South Korean won hit a fresh four-year low in weaker Asia on Tuesday as the U.S. dollar rose against the euro due to fears of a euro zone slowdown, while renewed concerns over credit markets stoked risk aversion.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar climbed towards a six-month high against the euro <EUR=> as investors waited for European data releases later in the day for evidence of the health of the euro zone economy. The dollar also neared a two-year high against the pound <GBP=D4> hit on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The South Korean won <KRW=> fell by 1 percent to 1,089.40 per dollar, its weakest since mid-November 2004, as investors increased their short won positions on growth worries, undeterred by a prospect of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Since the market sees that government actions are now useless, everybody is on the (dollar) bid side," a trader in Seoul said.\par \par \uc2 South Korean authorities were suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks, but the won is still the biggest loser among the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , having lost 14 percent this year.\par \par \uc2 In Malaysia, traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted selling dollars to put a floor under the ringgit <MYR=>.\par \par \uc2 The ringgit fell as low as 3.393 per dollar to hit a nine-month low against the dollar, hurt by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision on Monday to leave rates on hold despite rising inflation.\par \par \uc2 "CPI is so high but they haven't done anything to contain the inflation while other central banks in Asia are hiking rates," said one trader in Kuala Lumpur.\par \par \uc2 "And there is the Anwar election today. A lot of event risk," he said, referring to a by-election that opposition leader Anwar Ibrahim is contesting as he seeks to return to parliament.\par \par \uc2 MORE \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Traders in the Philippines also suspected authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the peso <PHP=>, which fell 0.8 percent to an 11-month low of 46 against the broadly stronger dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the market at 45.88 and 45.98 per dollar, and now they are defending 46," a trader in Manila said.\par \par \uc2 Two other traders in Manila also confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I think there's still demand for dollars. The market would rather hold dollar than peso," a second trader said.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  said they were watching several factors to determine \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement in the region.\par \par \uc2 "For the rest of the week the focus will mainly be on testing key \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels, the political theatre in Malaysia and \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meetings in Thailand and the Philippines, and slowing growth indicators," they said in a note.\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> extended early losses and dipped 0.6 percent to 1.4263 as market players speculated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may shift its monetary policy away from battling inflation towards one more supportive of growth. "There is a lot of talk that the authorities may change the policy in October," a Singapore-based trader said. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at   0740 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       109.74         109.94       +0.18\par  Sing dlr        1.4241         1.4173       -0.48\par  Taiwan dlr      31.552         31.430       -0.39\par  Korean won     1088.50        1078.90       -0.88\par  Baht             34.24          34.09       -0.44\par  Peso             46.00          45.65       -0.76\par  Rupiah         9173.00        9154.00       -0.21\par  Rupee            44.00          43.78       -0.50\par  Ringgit         3.3900         3.3730       -0.50\par  Yuan            6.8526         6.8481       -0.07\par  Change so far in 2008\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       109.74         111.33       +1.45\par  Sing dlr        1.4241         1.4382       +0.99\par  Taiwan dlr      31.552         32.443       +2.82\par  Korean won     1088.50         935.70      -14.04\par  Baht             34.24          33.68       -1.64\par  Peso             46.00          41.28      -10.26\par  Rupiah         9173.00        9390.00       +2.37\par  Rupee            44.00          39.41      -10.43\par  Ringgit         3.3900         3.3050       -2.51\par  Yuan            6.8526         7.3041       +6.59\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Editing by Tomasz Janowski)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080829e48q000v0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
