\par\par \b \uc2 2nd UPDATE: Thai  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Ready To Hike At July Meeting\b0\par\par\uc2 598 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 2008\par 10:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds Governor's comment on baht, interest rates, Vietnam's dong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 By Phisanu Phromchanya\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Thailand is ready to take monetary policy action to tackle high inflation and doesn't believe a rate hike will hurt economic growth much, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's governor Tarisa Watanagase said Monday.\par \par \uc2 The hawkish comments will reinforce market expectations of an interest rate hike in the near future but Tarisa ruled out calling an early meeting of the Monetary Policy Committee. It's next slated to meet on July 16.\par \par \uc2 Any increase in the policy interest rate is unlikely to have a significant impact on spending or economic growth, Tarisa told reporters.\par \par \uc2 "Our real interest rate is negative, therefore if there is any hike in the policy interest rate, any affect on spending and economic growth won't be much," she said at a hastily-called press conference.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials last week said inflation could reach a double-digit level this year, creating worries among market participants that the bank would announce a surprise inter-meeting rate hike. The last time the Bank of Thailand changed the policy rate between meetings was after the Sept. 11, 2001 terrorist attacks in the U.S..\par \par \uc2 Thailand's benchmark interest rate has been unchanged at a growth-accommodative 3.25% since August last year to support an economy battered by the political troubles that culminated in the ouster of Thaksin Shinawatra as prime minister in a September 2006 coup.\par \par \uc2 Tarisa said financial markets have already responded to the signal sent by the last meeting of the MPC in May, when the committee warned it would tighten monetary policy if inflation continued to accelerate.\par \par \uc2 Major commercial banks raised key deposit and lending rates earlier this month while bond yields have risen sharply in anticipation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would raise the policy rate to dampen fast rising prices.\par \par \uc2 Inflation hit a decade high of 7.6% in May as record oil prices fed broad-based price increases.\par \par \uc2 The governor downplayed the chances of double-digit inflation. "It is possible that inflation may hit double digits in certain months depending on the movement in oil prices) but the chance is rather slim," she said.\par \par \uc2 The issues of whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should target headline inflation and whether it needs to change the inflation target band will be studied by a new MPC later this year, Tarisa said.\par \par \uc2 Membership of the MPC will change by the end of August following implementation of the recently passed Bank of Thailand Act\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  targets core inflation within a zero to 3.5% band.\par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  front, Tarisa said the baht has become more stable lately and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to ensure that it moves in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last week, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to limit the baht's depreciation and curb excessive volatility after noticing that foreign banks and offshore branches of local banks were speculating on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Tarisa said the recent baht weakness was due partly to portfolio outflows and concerns over domestic political instability.\par \par \uc2 The softer baht was in line with the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trend, with Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weighed by concerns over devaluation of the Vietnam dong and lower risk appetite amid expectations that U.S. rates have already reached their bottom, she said.\par \par \uc2 -By Phisanu Phromchanya, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com [ 16-06-08 0831GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080616e46g000g5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
