\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Thai cenbank says may  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  again on baht\b0\par\par\uc2 225 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2008\par 08:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Adds quotes, detail)\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, June 10 (Reuters) - Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it had stepped into the market to slow the baht's fall and would continue to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it remained volatile.\par \par \uc2  "We have acted on the volatility to keep the baht from getting too weak or too strong," Assistant Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Suchada Kirakul told reporters, confirming the bank had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a second straight day.  The baht hit a 5-month low of around 33.22 per dollar on Monday, but recovered to around 32.99 on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  "We still see some foreign speculation. From information gathered from banks, there have been three to four players," Suchada said.\par \par \uc2  She urged exporters and importers to stop aggravating the baht's volatility by speculating on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Suchada reiterated the BoT would focus mainly on interest rate policy to deal with rising inflation, although a stronger baht could help restrain rising retail prices fuelled by costly oil imports.\par \par \uc2  Thailand's annual inflation rate hit a 10-year high of 7.6 percent in May. [ID:nBKK311120]\par \par \uc2  (Reporting by Boontiwa Wichakul; Writing by Vithoon Amorn; Editing by Darren Schuettler)  \par \par \uc2 THAILAND-ECONOMY/BAHT (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080610e46a000e4\par }\page {\pa