\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 2-Asian central banks  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  to defend  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 536 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2008\par 08:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Central banks defend \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from capital outflows\par \par \uc2 * Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says speculators bet against baht\par \par \uc2 * Pressure mounts on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strong dollar and inflation\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, June 10 (Reuters) - Central banks in Thailand, India and South Korea stepped into markets once again on Tuesday to defend their falling \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from a rallying dollar and foreign capital outflows spurred by worries over inflation.\par \par \uc2 Two traders in Bangkok said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to help the baht recover from Monday's 5-month low of 33.41 per dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also sold dollars on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  persists," said a trader in Bangkok. "I think they want to repel speculators."\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  subsequently confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the baht's fall and would continue to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it remained volatile.\par \par \uc2 Up to four foreign speculators had tried to bet against the baht, Bank of Thailand Assistant Governor Suchada Kirakul told reporters.\par \par \uc2 The baht <THB=TH> rebounded to 32.93 per dollar, up about 0.9 percent from late Asian trade on Monday. It has fallen more than 3.5 percent in the past 3 weeks.\par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> jumped about 1 percent as two traders said the authorities were believed to be selling dollars. It hit levels as high as 1,020.9 per dollar, having at one point traded below 1,031.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India (RBI) \uc2 was seen selling dollars around 42.92 per dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened on concerns foreigners may pull out more from local stocks amid growing risk aversion.\par \par \uc2 The rupee <INR=IN> also recovered from an early low of 42.93, but stayed weaker than Monday's close of 42.87/88.\par \par \uc2 Philippine traders suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  there too had sold dollars to pull the peso <PHP=> back from 44.45 per dollar, its weakest since October.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unable to sustain its gains, ending local trade at 44.425 per dollar.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region have been under pressure from rising oil and commodity prices, which have highlighted the pressures on trade and fiscal balances and raised concerns monetary authorities are behind the curve on fighting inflation.\par \par \uc2 There was further selling pressure on the regionals on Tuesday from the dollar's broad rally driven by Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke's remarks on the dangers from inflation.\par \par \uc2 "We expect this (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to remain the main source of support for Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term, even if it may be temporary rather than a measure that will change the trend," \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  said in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 Lehman said there would, however, be a divergence among the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a worsening growth and inflation backdrop weighed on portfolio flows, with \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Singapore dollar and Taiwan dollar expected to fare better than some of the others. (Writing by Vidya Ranganathan; Editing by Jacqueline Wong) ((vidya.ranganathan@thomsonreuters.com; +65-68703090; Reuters Messaging: vidya.ranganathan.reuters.com@reuters.net))\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (WRAPUP 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|IF|Z|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080610e46a000cp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
