\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Thai BOT: No Unusual Inflows As Cap Controls Removed   \b0\par\par\uc2 502 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 04:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Bank of Thailand Governor Tarisa Watanagase said Tuesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw no unusual inflows following the removal of capital control measures the previous day, and she is satisfied with the results.   \par \par \uc2 "The effect of the removal of the controls isn't different from what we had expected and I'm satisfied with it," Tarisa said in a television program broadcast early Tuesday on the local Channel 9, run by the state-owned  \uc2 MCOT PCL\uc2  (MCOT.TH).   \par \par \uc2 After some initial volatility in government bonds, Thai markets reacted calmly to the elimination Monday of controls including a 30% withholding on short-term capital inflows and an exemption from the 30% rule for fully-hedged foreign investment in local debt.   \par \par \uc2 However, Tarisa warned that if necessary, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could impose the controversial measures again.   \par \par \uc2 "We have the measure right in our pocket. It is possible that we could impose it again if we find that necessary, although we have no intention to do so for now," she said.   \par \par \uc2 Assistant Governor Suchada Kirakul admitted late Monday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to smooth the transition, but Tarisa said in the interview that no unusual capital inflows had been detected.   \par \par \uc2 The governor said the baht weakened slightly on Monday in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , under pressure from widespread selling in global equities.   \par \par \uc2 Exporters did not resort to panic-selling of U.S. dollars after the removal of controls, while importers have been accumulating dollars, she said.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the dollar ended Monday at THB31.60 on the onshore market, up from THB31.50 late Friday due to aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Stock Exchange of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  index closed down 0.3% and bonds finished mostly flat after an initial flurry of buying. At 0341 GMT Tuesday, the dollar was at THB31.65, and the SET Index was up 0.3% at 845.00 points.   \par \par \uc2 Tarisa said some foreign funds did flow into local bonds Monday following the removal of controls.   \par \par \uc2 However, investors looking for Thai interest rates to fall didn't find anything in the governor's comments to support their hopes.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts had generally expected interest rates to drop in order to reduce pressure on the baht to appreciate, but a growing number are coming around to the view that rising inflation will limit the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's flexibility.   \par \par \uc2 Tarisa said Thailand's policy rate of 3.25% is already among the lowest in the region, and any decision on interest rates will be up to the Monetary Policy Committee, which will have to weigh inflation and economic risks as well as \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Consumer price index inflation accelerated to a 20-month high at 5.4% on year in February on rising prices of fuel and food. The MPC meets next on April 9.   \par \par \uc2 -By Phisanu Phromchanya, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com [ 04-03-08 0358GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080304e4340003t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
