\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Falls On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Despite Cap Control Removal   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Phisanu Phromchanya   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 828 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 12:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The baht fell against the U.S. dollar Monday but Thailand's other markets reacted calmly to the removal of controversial controls on short-term capital inflows.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended the day at THB31.60 on the onshore market, up from THB31.50 late Friday, thanks to aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on both the local and offshore markets, while the stock market closed down 0.3% and the bonds finished flat.   \par \par \uc2 Economists said markets had already factored in the end of the capital controls which was announced Friday and said the lifting of the measures wouldn't have a longer-term impact on Thailand's economy or markets either.   \par \par \uc2 "The reality is the thrust of the existing controls have already been blunted considerably and the removal is unlikely to provide any substantial economic lift,"  \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  said.   \par \par \uc2 The end of capital controls - first imposed in December 2006 - is leading to some convergence between the onshore and offshore baht exchange rate although a rally in the baht was prevented by hectic \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's assistant governor Suchada Kirakul said the bank stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Monday to smooth the baht's intraday direction.   \par \par \uc2 In late Asian trade, the U.S. dollar was quoted offshore at THB31.55-THB31.60 versus THB31.10 late Friday.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to be the only buyer supporting the dollar both in onshore and offshore markets," a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a foreign bank in Thailand said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday sent a circular to local banks asking them to avoid transactions that may involve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation to prevent excessive baht volatility.   \par \par \uc2 "The circular wasn't helping much to calm the baht, it's the massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that did the job," said a dealer at a local bank.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar is expected to be rangebound between THB31.50-THB31.70 in the near term.   \par \par \uc2 While analysts agree the two rates will eventually converge, some argue the offshore market may not disappear entirely given \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules that restrict baht liquidity and curb capital inflows.  \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may now attempt to enforce a less clearly delineated two-tier \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.   \par \par \uc2 Stock Market Looking Overseas   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Thailand's main stock index closed down 0.3% at 842.92 points, off its intraday high of 849.49.   \par \par \uc2 "Sentiment was dampened by losses in external bourses. However, our performance is still considered good in relative to regional markets," said Bualuang Securities strategist Chaiyaporn Nompitakcharoen.   \par \par \uc2 "We could say that the (removal of capital control) measure did help limit our loss today."   \par \par \uc2 The SET Index is expected to move in a tight range between 840-850 points Tuesday with traders still cautious about the health of U.S. economy and its financial sector. However, optimism over the Thai government's economic stimulus package - expected to be announced Tuesday -is expected to limit any downside, he said.   \par \par \uc2 Thai government bonds rallied in early trading, dragging yields down by 15 basis points, thanks to buying from foreign investors now that their local bond investment is no longer subject to capital controls.   \par \par \uc2 "The removal of reserve requirement rules had a positive impact onthe bond market and we have seen some foreign players starting to accumulate short-term bonds," said local bond dealer.   \par \par \uc2 However, early gains were later erased as profit taking kicked in following the release of inflation data, which dimmed hopes for a quick interest rate cut. That is likely to prevent any big fall in yields going forward.   \par \par \uc2 Thailand's inflation rate rose to a 20-month high of 5.4% in February due to higher food and fuel prices. The core consumer price index, which strips out volatile food and energy prices, rose 1.5% in February from the same month a year earlier.   \par \par \uc2 High oil prices, a healthy recovery in domestic consumption and investment and the government's expansionary fiscal policy is likely to fuel inflation in coming months too.   \par \par \uc2 "The key question now is whether fears of a strong baht would prompt the BOT (Bank of Thailand) to cut rates and how far the government would go in pressuring the BOT to cut rates. Our stance is that the BOT should not cut now and probably doesn't want to cut either," DBS said in a report Monday.   \par \par \uc2 The decision to remove the capital controls came within weeks of the formation of Thailand's first elected government since the September 2006 coup that ousted Thaksin Shinawatra as prime minister.   \par \par \uc2 During campaigning for the Dec. 23 elections, the pro-Thaksin People Power Party, which now leads a six-party coalition, vowed to abolish the controls to boost Thailand's reputation with foreign investors.   \par \par \uc2 -By Phisanu Phromchanya, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2266 0744; phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 (Supunnabul Suwannakij and Piyarat Setthasiriphaiboon contributed to this article) [ 03-03-08 1124GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080303e433000n9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
