\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Fin Min: Investors Have Reacted Calmly To Cap-Control Removal   \b0\par\par\uc2 175 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 04:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Thai Finance Minister Surapong Suebwonglee said Monday that investors have reacted calmly to the removal of capital controls, announced by the Bank of Thailand late Friday.   \par \par \uc2 As of 0345 GMT, the Stock Exchange of Thailand Index barely changed at 845.41 points, down 0.35 point. The U.S. dollar rose to THB31.58 as at 0345 GMT from THB31.50 late Friday on aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said dealers.   \par \par \uc2 However, Surapong said he had no information on whether the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market today.   \par \par \uc2 He said the baht is likely to stay volatile for a week after the abolishment of capital controls before it could return to move at a similar pace with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of Thailand are closely monitoring the movement of the baht, said Surapong.   \par \par \uc2 -By Bangkok Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com [ 03-03-08 0353GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080303e4330003v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
