\par\par \b \uc2 INSTANT VIEW 2-Thailand to lift capital controls   \b0\par\par\uc2 834 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Februar 2008\par 11:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Feb 29 (Reuters) - Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it would lift capital controls imposed in December 2006 to rein in the baht <THB=TH> , with effect from March 3.   \par \par \uc2 The offshore rate for the baht immediately moved closer to the onshore rate in reaction to the news.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ****************************************************************\par  **    KEY POINTS:\par  -- The Bank of Thailand's governor said economic recovery\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 allowed the controls to be lifted.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For details, click [nBKT000594] [nBKT000595] [nBKT000596]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 COMMENTARY:   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USARA WILAIPICH, ECONOMIST, STANDARD CHARTERED BANK:   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Markets are playing on a possible lifting of capital controls. A gap between offshore and onshore markets is narrowing with the expectations and people think the cutting of policy interest rateS by the Bank of Thailand is underway." KOSIN SRIPAIBOON, HEAD OF RESEARCH AT UOB KAYHIAN SECURITIES:   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Overall, it should be positive to the country as it will attract more money inflows, but the lifting should hurt exports and imports and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should have measures to help.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The lifting comes at a time when the government is planning to hold roadshows soon. The government wants to restore foreign investor confidence. We should see more money inflows into both stock and bond markets, as well as direct investments.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The index rose instantly after the Bank of Thailand planned to hold a conference, rising from 838 to go through 840 points.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It should lift the main index further, but just in the short term, as investors have already priced in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's planned announcement."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KONGKIAT OPASWONGKARN, CHIEF EXECUTIVE, ASIA PLUS SECURITIES:   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Finally, the day we've been waiting for has come.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Like everyone else, the lifting is no surprise. The government made it clear they would lift it even before they got elected."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "For a starter, the controls are not working. If they had really worked, the baht had to be weaker than this. Second, it's something totally opposite to the pro-growth policy of the government.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "What's next is what the government would do with the Foreign Business Act. The stock market should react positively to this next week, but I don't think there'll be a dramatic surge."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SEAN CALLOW, STRATEGIST, WESTPAC BANK, SINGAPORE:   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Very much welcomed and not before time, mind you.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I think the relatively anti-business, anti-foreign attitude of the military-appointed government has ensured that there is no flood of foreign capital ready to pour back into Thailand.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "But a positive step nonetheless, a win for the new government.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I wonder if there will be any accompanying measures to help exporters."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CALLUM HENDERSON, HEAD OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STRATEGY, STANDARD CHARTERED BANK, SINGAPORE:   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Offshore will converge towards the onshore price.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Details are unclear at this point, in terms of the URR and the special accounts, what has been scrapped and what is still    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par there. For now the market assumes everything is gone -- that\par may not necessarily be right -- and onshore baht will converge\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to offshore baht."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CLAUDIO PIRON, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STRATEGIST AT JPMORGAN IN SINGAPORE:   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The obvious move is underway - that is the convergence between offshore baht toward the onshore rate, driven by the prospect of renewed access to onshore liquidity.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The wider implication is that Thailand will reenter in to investable bond indices, such as  \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's GBI-EM local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixed income index.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The resultant inflows could cause the local bond curve to flatten. The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can of course be expected to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  accumulation already running at 30 percent in a year-on-year terms.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Also note last statement that they have alternative measures to stabilise the baht. So there may yet be a twist in the tail.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MARKET:   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - The baht weakened in offshore trading, moving closer to the onshore levels for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In offshore deals, the baht <THB=W> moved to 30.90 per dollar from the day's highs of 29.70 and levels near 30.05 before the announcement.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In onshore trading, the baht <THB=TH> moved up to 31.35 from levels of 31.90 prior to the Bank of Thailand press conference.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BACKGROUND   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - The capital controls were imposed in December 2006 to curb speculation in the baht, which rose 14 percent against the dollar that year. It rose another 7 percent in 2007 despite the controls and has risen 5 percent so far this year.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - The controls led to the emergence of a two-tier market in the baht, one onshore <THB=TH> and one offshore <THB=W>. The baht was firmer in the offshore market.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - The controls required in particular that 30 percent of all \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  inflows without underlying business deals should be deposited with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , interest free, for a year.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - The stock exchange fell nearly 15 percent in immediate reaction to the controls, the market's biggest one-day fall, prompting the Bank of Thailand quickly to exempt equity investments. Other exemptions followed in time.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 THAILAND-ECONOMY/CONTROLS (VIEW 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ABX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080303e42t000t6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
