\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia mostly up, Singapore dollar at 11-year high   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Melissa Chia   \par \uc2 743 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2008\par 05:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Feb 22 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose on Friday amid expectations of further U.S. interest rate cuts, with the Singapore dollar hitting an 11-year peak, the Thai baht at a 10-1/2-year high and the Taiwan dollar at a 2-1/2-year high.   \par \par \uc2 The rate outlook overshadowed more bearish news on the U.S. economy in the shape of the Philadelphia Federal Reserve's business index for February, which showed an unexpectedly deep contraction in activity.   \par \par \uc2 "Looks as though dollar weakness is outweighing risk aversion," said Sean Callow, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at  \uc2 Westpac Banking Corporation.\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> rose 0.3 percent to hit an 11-year high of 1.4070 per dollar, but it met some resistance there despite traders' expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will allow further gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help contain inflation.   \par \par \uc2 One trader in Singapore said its rise was checked by fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although he suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) had not yet \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "I think MAS might be looking to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , just as there was some suspicion of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 1.41 earlier this week," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Inflation in Singapore hit a 25-year high of 4.4 percent in December, leaving the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a dilemma as it has to balance the need to control inflationary pressures with slowing economic growth.   \par \par \uc2 "Do I let the Singapore dollar run rampant to cool off imported inflation? Or do I try to weaken it to help my sagging domestic exports, which are only going to get worse with each bad print in U.S. economic numbers?" said a dealer in Singapore.   \par \par \uc2 Inflation data for January is due on Monday and analysts at DBS expect a further jump to 6.6 percent due to increased transport, food and oil costs.   \par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=TH> hit a 10-1/2-year high of 32.30 per dollar in onshore trading, and traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been buying dollars to halt a rise fuelled by rising export receipts.   \par \par \uc2 "The reality is that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively to counter appreciation pressure that has switched away from capital flows into current account surplus pressure," analysts at  \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  said in a note.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tops the list of gainers in the region for 2008, having risen 4.2 percent so far this year.   \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> climbed as far as 31.30 per U.S. dollar, its highest since June 2005, a day after Taiwan announced higher-than-expected fourth-quarter GDP growth.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also been helped by recent government initiatives to improve relations with China, including a proposal to allow mainland Chinese to buy property in Taiwan and for local firms to invest more in China,  \uc2 UBS\uc2  said in a report.   \par \par \uc2 "The resurgence of economic reform initiatives and efforts to improve economic linkages with China should be positive for the Taiwan dollar, in our view,"  \uc2 UBS\uc2  said. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par DOLLAR  Change on the day at   0756 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       107.29         108.10       +0.75\par  Sing dlr        1.4063         1.4109       +0.33\par  Taiwan dlr      31.300         31.521       +0.71\par  Korean won      948.40         948.20       -0.02\par  Baht             32.32          32.44       +0.37\par  Peso             40.65          40.63       -0.05\par  Rupiah         9170.00        9172.00       +0.02\par  Rupee            39.95          39.93       -0.05\par  Ringgit         3.2160         3.2200       +0.12\par  Yuan            7.1435         7.1413       -0.03\par  Change so far in 2008\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       107.29         111.33       +3.77\par  Sing dlr        1.4063         1.4382       +2.27\par  Taiwan dlr      31.300         32.443       +3.65\par  Korean won      948.40         935.70       -1.34\par  Baht             32.32          33.68       +4.21\par  Peso             40.65          41.28       +1.56\par  Rupiah         9170.00        9390.00       +2.40\par  Rupee            39.95          39.41       -1.34\par  Ringgit         3.2160         3.3050       +2.77\par  Yuan            7.1435         7.3041       +2.25 (Reporting\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 by Melissa Chia; Editing by Alan Raybould)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080225e42m0007i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
