\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia gains, Thailand denies policy change   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Vidya Ranganathan   \par \uc2 823 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2007\par 05:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Dec 4 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed some light gains on Tuesday and regional stock markets also rose despite increasing market jitters about the U.S. mortgage sector.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was supported by expectations the Federal Reserve will cut rates by as much as half a percentage point when it meets on Dec. 11, therefore providing support to the economy.   \par \par \uc2 But risk aversion was heightened, causing high-yielders such as the Aussie dollar to fall, amid mounting concerns that already tight short-term money markets will get squeezed further as the year-end approaches.   \par \par \uc2 Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy was in focus on Tuesday after a newspaper report that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had shifted policy from a managed float to guiding the baht against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  denied the report.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <THB=TH>, which offshore players barely trade after last year's imposition of capital controls, stayed steady around 33.84 per dollar, showing almost no reaction to the report.   \par \par \uc2 But the report in the Nation English-language newspaper initially raised some concerns among analysts about how policy makers could possibly manage the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a trade-weighted basket when they already have an inflation-targeting monetary objective.   \par \par \uc2 Claudio Piron of JPMorgan Chase Bank said it seemed the baht's trade-weighted index had moved in a 4.2 percent wide band since September.   \par \par \uc2 "It is currently at the upper limit of this range. This would imply that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  now to prevent any further baht strength against \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.   \par \par \uc2 RISK APPETITE SAGS   \par \par \uc2 Other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied, even though the Japanese yen <JPY=> was underpinned by an unwinding of risky carry trades funded using the low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Stock markets in most parts of Asia, barring Malaysia and Japan, were higher but just marginally. MSCI's measure of Asia Pacific stocks excluding Japan <.MIAPJ0000PUS> was up 0.22 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Asian high-yielders, the Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> and Philippine peso <PHP=>, gained 0.6 percent each with the latter hitting a fresh 7-\u189\'00\'BD year high of 42.12 per dollar despite talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap its rise.   \par \par \uc2 The rupiah rose to the firmer side of 9,300 per dollar for the first time in two weeks. The South Korean won <KRW=> was steady in a 922-925 per dollar range.   \par \par \uc2 The won has been undermined by a shortage of dollar funding in Korea after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's curbs during the past year to limit short-term foreign borrowings.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts say short-term funding has been scarce in several other places, such as India, China and Indonesia, and is putting downward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as foreign investors unwind bond and equity holdings and repatriate their dollars. "Our risk appetite index is in risk aversion, which would usually mean a sharp sell off in emerging markets," said Callum Henderson, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Standard Chartered Bank.   \par \par \uc2 "The fact that is not happening yet should suggest reduced liquidity," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Interbank lending rates in sterling soared to 9-year highs on Monday as banks struggled to secure cash for the year end in markets grappling with the fallout of the U.S. subprime mortgage problems on credit. And a European monetary policy maker warned of even tighter conditions to come. [nL03366111]. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0823 GMT    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       110.30         110.54       +0.22\par  Sing dlr        1.4472         1.4510       +0.26\par  Taiwan dlr      32.305         32.318       +0.04\par  Korean won      922.40         924.90       +0.27\par  Baht             33.84          33.83       -0.03\par  Peso             42.07          42.30       +0.55\par  Rupiah         9296.00        9352.00       +0.60\par  Rupee            39.42          39.49       +0.18\par  Ringgit         3.3420         3.3590       +0.51\par  Yuan            7.3982         7.4033       +0.07\par  Change so far in 2007\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       110.30         119.01       +7.90\par  Sing dlr        1.4472         1.5337       +5.98\par  Taiwan dlr      32.305         32.585       +0.87\par  Korean won      922.40         929.50       +0.77\par  Baht             33.84          36.08       +6.62\par  Peso             42.07          49.03      +16.54\par  Rupiah         9296.00        8988.00       -3.31\par  Rupee            39.42          44.26      +12.27\par  Ringgit         3.3420         3.5270       +5.54\par  Yuan    