\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Thai MOF Says Baht, Fiscal Policies Need Harmony   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Phisanu Phromchanya   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 513 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2007\par 10:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Thailand's Finance Minister Chalongphob Sussangkarn has put the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on notice to keep the baht under control, warning that expansionary fiscal policy will require the exchange rate to be actively managed.   \par \par \uc2 He also made a veiled call for greater cooperation between the finance ministry and the Bank of Thailand, saying that monetary and fiscal policies must work in harmony.   \par \par \uc2 "If we were to stimulate the economy by using fiscal policy, then we need to strongly manage the exchange rate. We can't simply let it move along with market forces," Chalongphob told a Fiscal Policy Office seminar.   \par \par \uc2 Higher government spending would lead to higher interest rates, which would attract more capital inflows and cause the baht to appreciate, hurting export competitiveness and economic growth, he said.   \par \par \uc2 The army-appointed government has recently said it will accelerate major infrastructure projects in the fourth quarter to spur Thailand's sluggish economy. The government is also planning a budget deficit of THB165 billion ($4.8 billion)in the 2008 fiscal year starting October 1.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers say the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has continuously \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in recent weeks to curb the baht's appreciation. In the onshore market, the U.S. dollar has traded in a tight range of THB34.20-THB34.30 over the past week.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had difficulty controlling the baht in July when an influx of foreign money into the stock market propelled the unit to a fresh 10-year high against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Trying to ease concerns about damage to the export sector and big job losses, the government liberalized capital outflows in the hope this would stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise.   \par \par \uc2 Chalongphob said it's important that the government's fiscal and monetary policies work in harmony. "If both policies don't go along, then they won't be effective."   \par \par \uc2 An amendment to public debt management law, which will soon be sent to the National Legislative Assembly, will allow the finance ministry to take a greater role in maintaining a stable exchange rate, he said.   \par \par \uc2 Once enacted, the ministry will be able to issue bonds for the purpose of debt market development, even when there is no budgetary necessity.   \par \par \uc2 The proceeds could be used to invest in domestic and offshore securities, providing another tool for management of the exchange rate, Chalongphob said.   \par \par \uc2 The government's decisions about whether to fund large infrastructure projects domestically or from overseas should also take into account the impact on the baht, which hit a 10-year high in July, he said.   \par \par \uc2 The government is also working on an amendment to the Act governing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 It will require the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to submit its monetary policy framework for Cabinet approval so that the overall direction of fiscal and monetary policy is the same, the minister said.   \par \par \uc2 -By Phisanu Phromchanya, Dow Jones Newswires; 662 266 0744; phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Stephen Wright [ 17-09-07 0822GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070917e39h000cz\par }\page {\par\fs20{