\par\par \b \uc2 IMF chief says Asian economies stronger than in 1997   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Vithoon Amorn   \par \uc2 555 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 2007\par 14:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, July 28 (Reuters) - The International Monetary Fund said on Saturday it saw no immediate risks of a financial crisis for Asian economies hit in recent months by a heavy influx of global capital.   \par \par \uc2 Asian countries should employ a combination of measures to manage huge inflows of foreign funds and exploit them for accelerating their economic expansion, IMF Managing Director Rodrigo Rato said.   \par \par \uc2 "Capital inflow is certainly a worldwide phenomenon. For Asian economies, that reflects a lot of things including increased liquidity and growing attractiveness of the economies. I believe that is good news," Rato told a news conference.   \par \par \uc2 Since late last year, Thailand has struggled to discourage capital inflows which have fuelled the baht's rise to 10-year highs against the dollar and eroded its export competitiveness.   \par \par \uc2 "I don't think right now Thailand and Asia have reasons to expect any crisis. Volatility is a problem and not desirable but that doesn't necessarily bring us to a crisis," Rato said.   \par \par \uc2 "Macro-economic fundamentals are stronger now than they were 10 years ago. Exchange rate flexibility also plays a very important role and the integration of Asian economies into the world economy is stronger," he said, referring to the 1997 Asian economic crisis.   \par \par \uc2 In a speech delivered to a meeting of Asian central bankers on Saturday, Rato urged China and other Asian countries to relax their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.   \par \par \uc2 "Greater exchange rate flexibility is not only in China's best interest but would allow other Asian countries to appreciate with less concern about competitiveness," he said.   \par \par \uc2 "There is also the possibility of such protectionism spinning out of control with disastrous consequences for the global economy," Rato said.   \par \par \uc2 DIFFERENT APPROACH   \par \par \uc2 China manages the value of its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also called the renmimbi, within a narrow range that the United States and many European countries maintain does not represent its fair value given China's rising global economic might.   \par \par \uc2 Thailand imposed tough capital controls last December to try to keep foreign capital out but has since relaxed most of them after they proved ineffective in slowing the baht's gains.   \par \par \uc2 Despite active \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and measures taken by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stall its gains, the baht has appreciated about 7 percent against the dollar this year after rising nearly 14 percent in 2006.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  adopted a different approach last week to ease upward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by allowing more capital outflows, a move welcomed by the IMF chief.   \par \par \uc2 "Stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not be seen as a danger. It makes easier monetary policy and makes it easier to keep inflation targets in check. It attracts more foreign confidence in the economies," he told reporters.   \par \par \uc2 Rato said while appreciating Thailand's reasons to resort to capital controls last year, the measures were not a solution.   \par \par \uc2 "Experiences show capital controls are more and more short-lived in terms of benefits for the country. They certainly have all the drawbacks if made to last longer," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Bank of Thailand Governor Tarisa Watanagase on Saturday asked IMF officials for advice on how to cope with adverse market volatility arising from fast flows of global capital.   \par \par \uc2 ASIA-IMF/CAPITAL|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ABX|BNX|FUN|Z|SI|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070728e37s0009x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
