\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia mostly firmer, peso jumps after rate cut   \b0\par\par\uc2 847 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2007\par 05:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, July 13 (Reuters) - Rising Asian shares buoyed most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday with the Philippine peso leading the pack after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slashed interest rates but eased the impact by scrapping a low-interest deposit scheme.   \par \par \uc2 The peso <PHP=> steadied near 45.75 per dollar, up half a percent from Thursday's close, after suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed it back from a day high of 45.73.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate cut yesterday seems to be taken in a positive light," a trader in Manila said. "The cut is positive for the equity market, and with the equity market strong, there is foreign interest and that causes the peso to strengthen," he said.   \par \par \uc2 The Philippine shares <.PSI> rose about 0.8 percent on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised investors by cutting its key rates by 150 and 175 basis points.   \par \par \uc2 In an accompanying move, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  removed a tiered scheme, under which interest rates were reduced by up to 400 basis points on banks' deposits in excess of 10 billion pesos.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Amando Tetangco said the combined impact of the two decisions would be neutral, but some analysts believed the moves still amounted to moderate easing.   \par \par \uc2 "While easing is bullish for the government bonds we expect a limited negative impact on the peso as strong economic fundamentals will continue to attract capital inflows to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," analysts at ING said in a research note.   \par \par \uc2 Sean Callow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Westpac, said he believed the relaxation was compatible with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's cut of its 2007 inflation forecast to 2.6-3.1 percent from 4-5 percent.   \par \par \uc2 "Markets should quickly factor in at least one rate cut in coming months," he said in a note.   \par \par \uc2 "While this will of course undermine the peso from a yield spread view, foreign equity investors already attracted to the Philippines' macro story are likely to become even more enthusiastic," he said.   \par \par \uc2 STOCKS RALLY   \par \par \uc2 MSCI's measure of Asia Pacific stocks excluding Japan climbed 1.6 percent to a record high, having risen in 11 of the past 12 sessions.   \par \par \uc2 Asian investors are more confident that the woes in the U.S. subprime mortgage market are unlikely to have any fallout on the region, given its good economic health.   \par \par \uc2 The South Korean won <KRW=> touched a fresh seven-month high at 915.20 per dollar on expectations of further interest rate rises after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its key rate by a quarter point on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=>, which has recently moved largely in tandem with the peso, rose as far as 9,010 per dollar, up about 0.4 percent from late Asia trade on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have strengthened broadly against the dollar so far this year, led by a 9.4 percent jump in the Indian rupee <INR=IN> and a 8.4 percent rise in the Thai baht <THB=TH>.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee rose moderately to 40.45 per dollar amid concerns that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap its gains, while the Thai baht was little changed at about 33.30 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Thai Finance Minister Chalongphob Sussangkarn said on Friday the government would meet representatives of the private sector next week to talk about the baht's surge to 10-year highs against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tried in vain to slow the baht's rise through capital controls and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "Owing to stronger portfolio investments into \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  on hopes of a recovery and a faster return to democracy, it appears that Thailand would have a more difficult time compared to India in managing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility," DBS analysts said in a note. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0844 GMT    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       122.29         122.04       -0.20\par  Sing dlr        1.5142         1.5156       +0.09\par  Taiwan dlr      32.762         32.793       +0.09\par  Korean won      916.70         918.10       +0.15\par  Baht             33.29          33.31       +0.06\par  Peso             45.70          45.98       +0.61\par  Rupiah         9028.00        9050.00       +0.24\par  Rupee            40.45          40.50       +0.12\par  Ringgit         3.4435         3.4535       +0.29\par  Yuan            7.5713         7.5673       -0.05\par  Change so far in 2007\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       122.29         119.01       -2.68\par  Sing dlr        1.5142         1.5337       +1.29\par  Taiwan dlr      32.762         32.585       -0.54\par  Korean won      916.70        0929.50       +1.40\par  Baht           