\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Thai BoT:Can't Return To Fixed  \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange \highlight\uc2  Rate   \b0\par\par\uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2007\par 09:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds additional comments by the governor and the baht exchange rate)   \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Bank of Thailand Governor Tarisa Watanagase said Wednesday that the country can't afford to return to a fixed exchange rate system, as she rejected calls by some exporters for drastic measures to stem the baht's rise to 10-year highs.   \par \par \uc2 "There are an enormous amount of funds out there in the global economy. To fix the exchange rate, we would need adequate foreign reserves, otherwise we wouldn't make it and that's the situation we faced 10 years ago," Tarisa said in a live interview broadcast on local television Channel 3.   \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Thailand was forced to float the baht in a move that triggered the Asian financial crisis of 1997 after spending all of its reserves in a failed defense of a fixed exchange rate mechanism.   \par \par \uc2 Since then, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has used a managed float system.   \par \par \uc2 Tarisa said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not have a targeted \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate since it largely depends on capital inflows.   \par \par \uc2 "We can't defend (the baht exchange rate) at a certain level. What we can do is prevent excessive volatility," Tarisa said.   \par \par \uc2 Tarisa said she expects upward pressure on the baht to decline in the second half of the year as exports are expected to slow while imports are tipped to rise.   \par \par \uc2 She said the recent baht's rise was due mainly to portfolio inflows into the stock market, and that the phenomenon should be only temporary.   \par \par \uc2 Later Wednesday, Tarisa told reporters that dollar selling by exporters has eased and returned to a normal level, but the baht was still under pressure to appreciate from persistent portfolio inflows.   \par \par \uc2 The governor had said Tuesday that the baht's strength was "abnormal," due to panic-selling by exporters triggered by a misunderstanding of the bank's plan to allow certain nonresidents to tap onshore baht liquidity.   \par \par \uc2 At 0707 GMT, the U.S. dollar was at THB33.29, slightly off a fresh 10-year low of THB33.18 set earlier Wednesday, after suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 -By Phisanu Phromchanya and Supunnabul Suwannakij, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2266 0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com [ 11-07-07 0730GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070711e37b000bi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
