\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Thai exporter dollar sales boost baht-c.bank  \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 09:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds details)  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, March 14 (Reuters) - The recent rise of the Thai baht stems from continuing dollar sales by exporters and there is no need for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Tarisa Watanagase said on Wednesday. "The baht remains strong because exporters continue to sell dollars," Tarisa told reporters as the baht rose towards 35 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "There is no need to do anything special because it is the people in the country who sell the dollar," she said.  \par \par \uc2 Tough capital controls imposed in December, aimed at curbing the baht's rise, have spawned a two-tier onshore and offshore market for the baht.  \par \par \uc2 It was trading at 35.02/05 to the dollar onshore <THB=TH> at 0740 GMT, compared with 35.09/01 in the morning, when the BoT was thought to be buying small amounts of dollars, research firm Forecast said.  \par \par \uc2 It was traded at 32.85 offshore <THB=W>.  \par \par \uc2 Despite a series of mis-steps by the new government since a bloodless coup in September, the baht has remained strong. It rose 14 percent against the dollar last year, more than any other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and has risen another 3 percent this year.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to monitor the baht and believed that further easing of capital controls would not affect the baht or panic the market, Tarisa said.  \par \par \uc2 It has backtracked several times on the controls. The latest was an exemption for fully hedged foreign inflows invested in mutual funds, property funds and debt markets from March 15.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would discuss the controls with new Finance Minister Chalongphob Sussangkarn on Thursday, Tarisa said, without elaborating.  \par \par \uc2 Chalongphob is thought to favour further relaxation of the controls the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  imposed on Dec. 18, requiring 30 percent of foreign inflows to be held in reserve with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , interest free, for a year.  \par \par \uc2 MARKET-THAILAND/BAHT (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070314e33e000qw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
