\par\par \b \uc2 Thai govt backs BoT changes, analysts see more  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Vithoon Amorn   \par \uc2 447 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2007\par 12:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Feb 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's military-appointed government approved changes to the law governing the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday which analysts said could trigger more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and hasten the lifting of capital controls.   \par \par \uc2 The changes, which still need parliamentary approval, would give the BoT more discretion to adjust assets kept as part of foreign reserves, government spokesman Yongyudh Maiyalarp told reporters after a cabinet meeting.   \par \par \uc2 JP Morgan said it would allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reduce the frequency of reporting on its foreign reserve management.   \par \par \uc2 "By exonerating the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from reporting changes in its \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is free to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at will and without the concern that its losses will have to be booked under political scrutiny at year end," it said in a note to clients.   \par \par \uc2 The amendments meant the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would need to reassess the value of foreign reserves only once a month, Yongyudh said. The BoT currently announces changes once a week.   \par \par \uc2 Recent heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the bank to slow the baht's rise against the dollar has pushed Thai foreign reserves to record highs in recent months, reaching $67.5 billion on Feb. 16.   \par \par \uc2 The baht rose around 14 percent against the dollar last year, the most of any Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The surge in foreign reserves has forced the BoT to issue more domestic baht bonds this year to mop up excess liquidity in the domestic market to avoid stoking inflation.   \par \par \uc2 The BoT reported last week that it posted a book loss of $4.9 billion in 2006, stemming largely from its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the dominant dollar portion of foreign reserves depreciated in value last year.   \par \par \uc2 JP Morgan said the changes could speed up a decision to lift tough capital controls imposed on Dec. 18 to rein in the baht.   \par \par \uc2 They require foreigners bringing in funds without underlying business to put 30 percent in interest-free bank accounts supervised by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for up to a year.   \par \par \uc2 The capital controls spawned a two-tier market for the baht.   \par \par \uc2 JP Morgan said the revision of the BoT law could help narrow a four percent spread between offshore and onshore baht rates.   \par \par \uc2 "Short-term \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  implication is that the offshore spot USD/THB rate will move higher in the event URR restrictions are lifted and liquidity returns," it said, referring to the 30 percent unremunerative required reserves.   \par \par \uc2 The baht traded offshore at around 34.15 per dollar at 1058 GMT on Tuesday, down from 33.80 late on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 THAILAND-ECONOMY/BANK|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070227e32r001gs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
