\par\par \b \uc2 PREVIEW-Thai Nov exports seen at 9-mth high despite baht rise  \b0\par\par\uc2 1,032 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 2006\par 07:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 * What: Bank of Thailand data on trade, manufacturing, others  \par \par \uc2 * When: Friday Dec. 29, 2.30 p.m. (0730 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 * Annual exports growth seen strongest in nine months  \par \par \uc2 By Vithoon Amorn  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Dec 27 (Reuters) - Thailand's exports in November are expected to have risen at their fastest annual pace in nine months, nudging trade and current account surpluses to new highs despite rises in the baht against the dollar, analysts say.  \par \par \uc2 Exporters saw their dollar earnings rise last month but expected smaller gains in baht terms, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to impose capital controls on Dec. 19 to slow Asia's fastest rising \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year.  \par \par \uc2 A Reuters survey of six analysts suggested the November current account surplus rose by about $1 billion from October to a record $1.88 billion.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Thailand is due to release November economic data on Friday, including trade, manufacturing and money supply.  \par \par \uc2 "Export growth will be considerably narrower in baht terms, closer to 8 percent, an indication of how exporters can indeed be squeezed as the USD-THB approached 35.0," said David Cohen, economist at Action Economics in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 He said the November surplus "might raise questions about the painfulness of this year's baht appreciation.  \par \par \uc2 The baht <THB=> rose about 2 percent against the dollar in November and had gained nearly 16 percent on the year before the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from breaking the psychological barrier of 35 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign investors recoiled at the capital controls which triggered a 15-percent plunge on the Thai stock market last week before the measures were rescinded for equity investments.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had to act before the baht did serious damage to the country's exports, which are equivalent to 60 percent of Thailand's gross domestic product.  \par \par \uc2 The baht was trading at 36.31 per dollar on Wednesday and was expected to remain subdued this week ahead of the New Year holidays.  \par \par \uc2 STRONG EXPORTS  \par \par \uc2 Analysts estimated November exports surged 21.1 percent from a year earlier, the biggest annual rise since February and topping a 20.9 percent increase in October.  \par \par \uc2 The impressive growth in November's exports was due partly to higher auto exports to Indonesia, said analyst Nujcharin Panarode at Capital Nomura Securities.  \par \par \uc2 Cars and auto parts are Thailand's second-biggest industrial exports after computers and electronics.  \par \par \uc2 The Manufacturing Production Index was expected to rise 6.3 percent in November from a year earlier, up from 5.4 percent in October.  \par \par \uc2 But some analysts questioned how long the good economic data could be sustained given signs of weaker domestic investment and consumption in the past few months.  \par \par \uc2 "On the whole, the November economic data should continue pointing to fundamental weakness. I believe the December data will likely be worse than November," said Leslie Khoo at Forecast Pte in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 BOT data showed annual private investment growth easing to 1.0 percent in October from average growth of 1.5 percent in the third quarter.  \par \par \uc2 Inflation data for December is due to be released at around 2 p.m. (0700 GMT) on Jan. 3.  \par \par \uc2 Poll details (pct change from year earlier, unless stated). All indicators refer to November, except for CPI which is for December)  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                MPI    Exp   Imp  Trade    C/A        CPI\par                                   $mln    $mln   Main   Core\par                                         (revised)  \par  Action                                   \par  Economics        7.0   21.0   3.0  1,500   1,850    3.5   \par 1.6\par  Capital Nomura   6.0   20.8   1.7  1,640   1,920    3.3   \par 1.4\par  Forecast         6.5   21.6   3.4  1,550   1,850    3.3   \par 1.6\par  IDEAglobal       6.0   20.3   3.3  1,400   1,800      ~     \par ~\par  Tisco Sec        5.5   21.1   1.7  1,679   1,909    3.4   \par 1.4\par  Kasikorn         \par  Research         8.0   21.8   2.5  1,662   2,012    3.6   \par 1.6\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par Median           6.3   21.1   2.8  1,595   1,880    3.4    1.6\par  Previous actual data:\par  2006\par  Nov               ~      ~      ~      ~       ~    3.5   \par 1.7\par  Oct              5.4   20.9   8.9    723     856    2.8   \par 1.8\par  Sep              5.7   14.5   9.1  1,402     826    2.7   \par 1.9\par  Aug              8.0   17.0  11.2    271     464    3.8   \par 1.9\par  Jul              6.3   17.7  16.3   -223     -40    4.4   \par 2.0\par  Jun              6.8   17.3   2.6   -425    -284    5.9   \par 2.7\par  May              8.8   18.7   9.1   -760   -1285    6.2   \par 2.7\par  Apr              4.1   11.5  -2.1   -520    -632    6.0   \par 2.9\par  Mar             10.1   15.8   2.1    187     136    5.7   \par 2.6\par  Feb             13.2   22.9  15.4    -24       ~    5.6   \par 2.7\par  Jan              5.8   14.8   0.5   -388       ~    5.9   \par 2.5\par  2005\par  Dec              6.1   11.7  26.0   -176       ~    5.8   \par 2.6\par  Nov              7.7   13.8  13.7   -201       ~    5.9   \par 2.4\par  Oct              7.9    7.7  20.2   -372       ~    6.2   \par 2.4\par  Sep             11.2 