\par\par \b \uc2 Thai baht fumble has long-term costs - S&P  \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Dezember 2006\par 05:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Dec 21 (Reuters) - Thailand's fumbled baht controls could trigger a further pull-out of foreign money and hurt domestic investment by driving up financing costs, ratings agency Standard & Poor's said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "Foreign investors will now be far more wary of investing in Thai financial markets," S&P credit analyst Kim Eng Tan said in a report two days after a bungled \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the rise of the baht sparked a huge share sell-off.  \par \par \uc2 "This will lead to higher funding costs in the Kingdom, with negative implications for the prices of debt and equity assets," Tan said.  \par \par \uc2 International investors slammed the measures, which were abruptly lifted for stock investments after the Thai bourse fell nearly 15 percent on Tuesday, its sharpest one-day loss in 16 years.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark stock index <.SETI> was down 2.66 percent at 0433 on Thursday after an 11.2 percent rebound on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 S&P said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls appeared to have put a brake on the baht, which fell to a one-month low against the dollar on Thursday as investors continued to dump the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But it noted "such success brings long-term costs".  \par \par \uc2 Domestic investment could become costlier if planned government spending led to a return of current account deficits, the report said.  \par \par \uc2 "This is because deficits would increase Thailand's reliance on foreign financing," it said.  \par \par \uc2 The interim government appointed after a bloodless Sept. 19 coup ousted Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra plans to boost public spending next year to keep the economy humming ahead of promised elections in late 2007.  \par \par \uc2 The surprise baht controls and later policy U-turn also tarnished the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reputation in the eyes of foreign investors, S&P said.  \par \par \uc2 "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained itself a reputation -- however undeserved -- as an \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one that administers abrupt and inconsistent policy actions," the report said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-THAILAND/S&P|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061221e2cl0007i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
