\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Mkts Make Partial Recovery On Baht Rule's Revision  \b0\par\par\uc2 1,141 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2006\par 11:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Thai markets stabilized Wednesday in a partial recovery following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to exempt stock and foreign direct investment inflows from the harsh reserve requirement it had placed on most capital inflows the previous day.  \par \par \uc2 The Stock Exchange of Thailand index closed 11.2% higher at 691.55 points, after panic selling pushed it down almost 15% to 622.14 at Tuesday's close.  \par \par \uc2 Many analysts said the botched implementation of rules designed to limit speculative pressures which have driven the baht to nine year highs have shattered foreign investors confidence, and will lead to sluggishness in Thai shares for a long time to come.  \par \par \uc2 The move came shortly after international fund managers had raised their weightings on Thai stocks, deeming that political tensions had eased in the wake of September's military coup that overthrew Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra.  \par \par \uc2 ABN Amro said in a report Wednesday that it has cut the recommended weighting of Thai shares in its Asia Ex-Japan portfolio to 1.5% from 2.5%, citing its view that uncertainty related to potential policy changes and elections due late next year will limit foreign inflows in the coming year.  \par \par \uc2 But Bank of Thailand Governor Tarisa Watanagase told reporters Wednesday that there were no signs yet that funds from the massive selling of Thai shares were flowing out of the country.  \par \par \uc2 And some fund managers said that although the event was unsettling, it didn't change the outlook for the companies whose shares they owned.  \par \par \uc2 "It is not an impressive sign of the thinking of the Thai government. But we are not changing Thailand's weighting in our portfolios," as fundamentals of Thai companies remain the same, said fund manager Hugh Young of Aberdeen Asset Management Asia Ltd.  \par \par \uc2 Tarisa said that due to the changes exempting equities-related inflows from the reserve requirement, the baht wouldn't fall as much as had earlier been expected.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed onshore trading at THB35.800, down from 35.915 at the Asian close Tuesday, but still up from a nine-year low early Monday at THB35.060.  \par \par \uc2 Deputy Finance Minister Sommai Phasee told reporters he expects the U.S. dollar to eventually settle around THB36-THB37.  \par \par \uc2 But Tarisa said Tuesday that the baht would eventually start to rise again due to broad dollar weakness in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, even if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to eliminate speculative forces allow the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drop back in line with its regional trading partners.  \par \par \uc2 The surging baht had prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to require as of Tuesday that onshore banks withhold for one year 30% of capital inflows that aren't trade- or services-related or those that aren't a repatriation of Thai residents' investments abroad.  \par \par \uc2 As of Wednesday, inflows to stocks and foreign direct investments were also exempted.  \par \par \uc2 For inflows still subject to the reserve, investors can request the entire amount withheld back after one year, or two-thirds of the amount withheld back in less than a year, resulting in an effective tax of 10% on the total initial investment.  \par \par \uc2 As inflows into bonds and other debt instruments are still subject to the withholding, Thailand's government bond market only stabilized Wednesday due to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought issues with terms of 10 years or more from primary dealers, calming a market that otherwise would have seen another day of losses in adjustment to a likely halt in speculative foreign demand.  \par \par \uc2 The bid yield of the benchmark 10-year bond due July 2016 ended at 5.11%, after rising 33 basis points to 5.20% on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Thailand's credit default swap spreads also recovered, narrowing to 25-to-30 basis points after widening sharply to 30-35 basis points on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Speculative Flows From Debt To Shares A Problem \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Finance Minister Pridiyathorn Devakula told The Wall Street Journal Asia on Wednesday that after the revision in the rules exempting equities-related inflows from the withholding requirement, the problem was to find a way to prevent speculative foreign money previously flowing into the debt market from moving into stocks.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tarisa said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may re-impose a THB300 million limit on total deposits by a single nonresident in onshore accounts, which was removed Tuesday so that foreigners selling shares could leave their funds in the country.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Suchart Sakkankosone, director of Exchange Control and Credits Department, said Wednesday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will announce "in one or two days" a plan to create a type of account through which nonresidents can buy and sell Thai shares.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Funds in foreigners' special equities-related accounts won't be allowed to shift into bonds or other assets, SET President Patareeya Benjapolchai said at a separate news conference Wednesday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Suchart said that when the accounts restricted to equities trading are created, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will restore the THB300 million limit on general nonresident accounts, but it hasn't been decided whether a limit will be imposed on the equities accounts.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, Tarisa rejected calls from many economists to scrap the attempts to control inflows via regulations and solve the problem by cutting interest rates instead.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We shouldn't use interest rates to solve the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  problem. The monetary policy committee has decided that now isn't the time for a rate cut," she said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Many economists expect the MPC to make a slight downward adjustment by setting its new benchmark, the one-day repurchase market rate, at 4.75% when it meets in January, after leaving the current 14-day benchmark rate at 5% when it met on Dec. 13.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But some economists believe Bank of Thailand may wait for the U.S. to lead the way before cutting the new one-day benchmark, because of its emphasis on inflation-targeting.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tarisa said the reason the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wouldn't use interest rates to manage the baht was that there is still a risk of higher inflation and the economy is growing at a reasonable pace.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cutting interest rates would also only attract more speculative inflows to debt instruments, which see capital gains when interest rates fall, and possibly to other markets if lower interest rates stimulated the economy, she said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation risks come from oil price instability and the tendency of the Ministry of Commerce to look for items to remove from the list of products controlled prices, Tarisa said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A ministry official said that the next meeting of the price committee is expected to be held in January, at which revisions to the list of controlled prices will be considered.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; tom.fox@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Supunnabul Suwannakij, Phisanu Phromchanya and Rattaphol Onsanit contributed to this story) [ 20-12-06 1001GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020061220e2ck0010n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
