\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Thai baht jumps, hits nine-year high  \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2006\par 02:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  (Updates with details, analyst comment)  \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Dec 12 (Reuters) - The Thai baht <THB=>, Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , jumped nearly 0.6 percent against the dollar in early trade on Tuesday and hit its strongest level in more than nine years.  \par \par \uc2  At 0224 GMT, the baht was quoted at 35.34 per dollar, extending its gains after strengthening beyond its previous high of 35.46 per dollar set in December 1998 and hitting its strongest level since early October 1997.  \par \par \uc2  Dealers at a major Thai commercial bank in Bangkok confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, but declined to comment further.  \par \par \uc2  Christy Tan, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Bank of America in Singapore, said markets were betting on a decision from the Bank of Thailand to keep interest rates unchanged on Wednesday, which would underpin the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2   "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is possible, but that will only slow the baht's rises and is unlikely to reverse the trend," she said.  \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meets on Wednesday to review its monetary policy, but 8 of 9 analysts surveyed by Reuters predicted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would leave its 14-day repurchase rate unchanged at 5.0 percent.  \par \par \uc2  The baht has gained 16 percent so far this year, despite Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and new anti-speculation measures announced last week.  \par \par \uc2  But Thai exporters have complained about the rise in the baht, worried it will crimp revenues and make their goods less competitive.  \par \par \uc2  The latest Reuters poll on positioning in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggests investors stepped up long positions in the Thai baht and remained bullish on the South Korean won and Singapore dollar.  \par \par \uc2  Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell on Monday thanks to a global rebound in the dollar and protracted concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but most analysts remain bullish about their near-term outlook, citing the region's solid economic fundamentals.    \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-THAILAND-BAHT (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061212e2cc0002f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
