\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia up, Thai baht rally sparks  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 739 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2006\par 05:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Dec 12 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars on Tuesday to rein in the baht as Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit its highest since the Asian financial crisis, while other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed its firm tone.  \par \par \uc2  The baht <THB=> retreated to 35.32 per dollar after reaching 35.23, its strongest since October 1997, strengthening beyond its previous high of 35.46 per dollar set in December 1998.  \par \par \uc2  Assistant governor at Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Suchada Kirakul, told reporters that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , buying dollars to try to slow the rise of the baht.  \par \par \uc2  But she said the bank would take time to consider whether fresh measures were needed to deter foreign speculation in the baht after it imposed curbs last week to block access by foreign speculators through domestic bond and debt paper transactions.  \par \par \uc2  A dealer at Bangkok Bank said he expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to impose new curbs to target \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation in the baht to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from breaching the key 35-per-dollar level.  \par \par \uc2  "A break below 35.00 could herald more selling, although we expect the BOT to guard this level religiously," said Thio Chin Loo, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at BNP Paribas.  \par \par \uc2  Christy Tan, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Bank of America in Singapore, said markets were betting on a decision from the Bank of Thailand to keep interest rates unchanged on Wednesday, which would underpin the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meets on Wednesday to review its monetary policy, but 8 of 9 analysts surveyed by Reuters predicted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would leave its 14-day repurchase rate unchanged at 5.0 percent.  \par \par \uc2  The baht has gained around 16.6 percent so far this year, prompting worries among local exporters that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise could crimp their revenues and make their goods less competitive.  \par \par \uc2  OPTIMISTIC  \par \par \uc2  Most analysts and dealers remain optimistic about the near-term outlook on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as capital flows into the region and trade surpluses persist, despite a wave of verbal and actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central banks to cap \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength.  \par \par \uc2  But some analysts believe \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the baht and the South Korean won, so far leading the rally, would probably lose pace while the Malaysian ringgit and Indian rupee were likely to outperform in the weeks ahead, since they have lagged the rally.  \par \par \uc2  The won <KRW=>, which led declines in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past two sessions, gained about a third of a percent on Tuesday to 922.4, with dollar purchases from exporters outweighing suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by local authorities.  \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> strengthened to as far as 3.538 per dollar, its highest level in nearly nine years, while the Philippine peso <PHP=> gained a fifth of a percent to 49.45.  \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar <SGD=> gained about a quarter of a percent to 1.54 per U.S. dollar, still off a nine-year high of 1.5362 struck last week.  \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> hovered between 32.41 and 32.55   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par per U.S. dollar on Tuesday. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change\par on the day at   0809 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       116.83         116.61       -0.19\par  Sing dlr        1.5400         1.5441       +0.27\par  Taiwan dlr      32.487         32.490       +0.01\par  Korean won      922.40         925.60       +0.35\par  Baht             35.32          35.55       +0.65\par  Peso             49.45          49.58       +0.26\par  Rupiah         9071.00        9090.00       +0.21\par  Rupee            44.83          44.80       -0.08\par  Ringgit         3.5375         3.5545       +0.48\par  Yuan            7.8298         7.8350       +0.07\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       116.83         117.96       +0.97\par  Sing dlr        1.5400         1.6625       +7.95\par  Taiwan dlr      32.487         32.850       +1.12\par  Korean won      922.40        1011.60       +9.67\par  Baht             35.32          41.11      +16.39\par  Peso             49.45          53.09       +7.36\par  Rupiah         9071.00        9835.00       +8.42\par  Rupee            44.83          45.04       +0.46\par  Ringgit         3.5375         3.7790       +6.83\par  Yuan            7.8298         8.0702       +3.07\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD  \