\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Ctrl Bk Asst Chief: Inflation Downtrend To Continue  \b0\par\par\uc2 478 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2006\par 08:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Bank of Thailand Assistant Governor Suchada Kirakul said Tuesday that inflation remains on a downward trend.  \par \par \uc2 The increase in consumer price index inflation in November to 3.5% on year from 2.8% in the previous month was due mainly to heavy flooding, she said.  \par \par \uc2 "Both CPI and core inflation are on a declining trend," Suchada said.  \par \par \uc2 Core inflation - based on the CPI but excluding volatile fresh food and energy prices - was up 1.7% on year, compared with 1.8% in October.  \par \par \uc2 However, comments last week from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Tarisa Watanagase indicated that the Bank of Thailand will wait until next year to lower interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to leave its 14-day repurchase target rate unchanged at 5.0%, when it holds its next policy meeting Wednesday. [ 12-12-06 0733GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Suchada also said the Thai baht is appreciating too quickly, buoyed by global dollar weakness and by capital inflows, but added that the baht's rise was also helping curb inflationary pressures.  \par \par \uc2 The baht has risen about 14% against the greenback this year, faster than the appreciation of other East Asian units, she said. But Suchada added that since the start of 2005, the baht has risen only 9.3% against the dollar, more or less in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Importers and debtors are benefitting from the baht's strength, she said.  \par \par \uc2 The negative effect on exporters, however, is limited, since exports are more affected by the economic strength of Thailand's trading partners than with the baht's value, she said.  \par \par \uc2 For every 1% rise in the baht's value against the dollar, export growth declines 0.1 percentage point, while for every one percentage point increase in the gross domestic product growth of trade partners, export growth rises 1.44 percentage points, she said.  \par \par \uc2 Suchada said the baht's strength is also allowing Thai businesses to improve or expand production by importing new machinery at a low cost.  \par \par \uc2 At 0748 GMT, the dollar was quoted at THB35.335 - off a nine-year low of THB35.250 hit earlier in the day - following suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a warning to speculators by Suchada that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still "taking care" of the baht.  \par \par \uc2 She didn't comment on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday or whether it planned to introduce any new measures to limit short-term capital inflows.  \par \par \uc2 She said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still evaluating the effectiveness of last week's move to ban short-term trading of local bonds by nonresidents and expanded restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps and loans between onshore and offshore financial institutions.  \par \par \uc2 -By Phisanu Phromchanya, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Michael Kitchen [ 12-12-06 0841GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020061212e2cc0007z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
